  "description": "MAJDOV crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C96 H132 Gd6 N6 O48,5(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd5 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.803-3.809 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 109.92-111.75°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C106H147Gd6N11O48.",
